Translation patch: `impl_from_value_num!` (`TryFrom<Value> for ParseIrOpt<$ty>`)

Change: `$ty::try_from(x).map(ParseIrOpt::Ready).map_err(|_| ..)` becomes `if <x in range> { Ok(ParseIrOpt::Ready(x as $ty)) } else { Err(..) }`, where for `x: i64` the range test is `($ty::MIN as i128) <= (x as i128) && (x < 0 || (x as u128) <= ($ty::MAX as u128))` and for `x: u64` it is `(x as u128) <= ($ty::MAX as u128)`.
Why: `TryFrom<i64>`/`TryFrom<u64>` for the integer types (and the blanket `TryFrom` via `From`) are not modelled by Aeneas.
Behaviour: Identical for every integer type `$ty`: `$ty::MIN as i128` and `$ty::MAX as u128` are exact (`MIN <= 0 <= MAX`, both within these types), `x as i128` and `x as u128` (for `x >= 0`) are exact, and a negative `x` is always below `MAX`; so the test holds exactly when `try_from` succeeds, and then `x as $ty` is the value it returns.

